From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PrismML-Eng <contact@prismml.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] llama : Prism runtime - ftype wiring, KV mean-centering, DSpark/DFlash

The llama-level half of the fork:

  - PQ2_0/PTQ1_0 ftype ids, names and row-data validation, plus detection
    of legacy group-128 Q2_0 files so they fail with a pointer to the right
    download instead of garbage output.
  - Per-channel K-cache mean-centering for Q4_0, with the hybrid-model and
    calibration-basis guards.
  - The Hadamard weight-fold runtime and its shared activation transform.
  - The DSpark / DFlash / DFly speculative-decoding drafters and the six
    hybrid-attention decode graph fusions.
  - The qwen35 ring decode path.

This is the patch most exposed to upstream churn: llama-arch.cpp alone is
479 added / 413 removed lines against a file upstream edits constantly.

Provenance
----------
Source:   https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp
Branch:   prism
Range:    5ea87ddad22541a37053c7ba92b02ec1923617c6..9a9394a895b96003ca842a6041cb28ac49a108f7
Base tag: b10615 (the fork's base is b10615 plus one unrelated webgpu commit,
          which is NOT included here - this diff is the fork's own work only)
Part 6 of 10, split by file group from the full 14,759-line fork diff.
llama.cpp is MIT licensed; the fork carries the same terms.
---
diff --git a/include/llama.h b/include/llama.h
index a04177f9f..deb1e1282 100644
--- a/include/llama.h
+++ b/include/llama.h
@@ -156,6 +156,9 @@ extern "C" {
         LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_NVFP4         = 39, // except 1d tensors
         LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_Q1_0          = 40, // except 1d tensors
         LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_Q2_0          = 41, // except 1d tensors
+        LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_PQ2_0     = 141, // except 1d tensors (Prism group-128 Q2_0; matches published PQ2_0 ggufs)
+        LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_PQ2_0_LEGACY = 142, // pre-rename value for the same format, still found in published ggufs
+        LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_PTQ1_0    = 143, // except 1d tensors (Prism group-128 ternary, 1.75 bpw)
 
         LLAMA_FTYPE_GUESSED = 1024, // not specified in the model file
     };
@@ -305,6 +308,10 @@ extern "C" {
     };
 
     struct llama_model_params {
+        // Opt-in DSpark head borrowing. Caller guarantees the bound target and keeps it alive
+        // until the drafter and all drafter contexts are destroyed. No head weights are copied.
+        const struct llama_model * dspark_head_source;
+
         // NULL-terminated list of devices to use for offloading (if NULL, all available devices are used)
         ggml_backend_dev_t * devices;
 
@@ -381,6 +388,14 @@ extern "C" {
         enum ggml_type type_k; // data type for K cache [EXPERIMENTAL]
         enum ggml_type type_v; // data type for V cache [EXPERIMENTAL]
 
+        // optional path to a per-layer K-cache mean-centering bias file (GGUF), or NULL to disable.
+        // the bias is subtracted from the K vector for each (kv-head, channel) right before it is
+        // written into the K cache, which improves quantization fidelity for GGML_TYPE_Q4_0 without
+        // changing attention results (the same constant is added to every logit in a query's row,
+        // which softmax is invariant to). currently only supported when type_k == GGML_TYPE_Q4_0.
+        // see tools/kv-mean-center to generate this file and docs/kv-mean-center.md for details.
+        const char * path_kv_mean_center;
+
         // Abort callback
         // if it returns true, execution of llama_decode() will be aborted
         // currently works only with CPU execution
